From d052902dc92f38cb80106e3d6acf101f359d024f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:14:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] perf(chat): release the stream's DB connection before
 awaiting the provider

stream_chat opens its own AsyncSessionLocal() and performs lookups on it
(ChatSession/project for billing, private-mode resolution, memory retrieval)
before calling the provider. Only persisted chats then committed, through
persister.prepare(); gateway, API-key and Private Mode turns kept that
autobegun transaction -- and with it one pooled connection and one PgBouncer
transaction-mode server slot -- open for the entire stream, which lasts
minutes. With DB_POOL_SIZE=12 + 20 overflow per worker, ~32 concurrent gateway
streams on one worker exhaust the pool (pool_timeout -> 500s) and 4 workers
starve PgBouncer's 90-slot default pool for every other query.

_end_request_transaction(db) commits (or rolls back) the stream's session
right before every acompletion() call, including the code-interpreter
follow-up iterations. Everything after the provider call already uses either
the persister (which commits per flush) or independent AsyncSessionLocal()
sessions for accounting, so no later code depends on the open transaction.

Test: tests/test_stream_releases_db_connection.py tracks the sessions
stream_chat creates and asserts none is in a transaction when the provider
is called; fails on the previous code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UTnpHajSmkk2JMLfuQoV7o
